Geany 2.1, mixed-link test 1 (riscos-gtk + riscos-crossdev 1.11-test1)
=====================================================================

A TEST, not a release. Geany is linked "mixed": UnixLib is inside the
program, as usual, but GTK 3.24.52, riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend and the
libraries under them (GLib, cairo, pango, harfbuzz, FreeType, fontconfig,
pixman, libpng, libjpeg...) are 26 shared libraries in !Geany.lib, loaded
by !SharedLibs (SOManager and ld-riscos/so/2) when Geany starts. Once
other GTK programs are built the same way they can share one copy of
those libraries instead of each carrying its own.

It has run on RISC OS 5.31 on Linux. This is its first try on RISC OS 5
running directly on the hardware.

You need
--------
- RISC OS 5 on ARMv7 or later (Pi 2 or later), 16 or 32 bpp mode
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv (PackMan),
  as for the normal GTK programs
- the !SharedLibs in this zip (from Iris: SOManager 3.04 with
  ld-riscos/so/2). The older !SharedLibs 4.0 from riscos.info has only
  ld-riscos/so/1 and can't run it; !Geany's !Run says so if that one is
  the one booted.

Trying it
---------
1. Copy the folder somewhere. If you already have a !SharedLibs in
   !Boot.Resources, keep a copy of it first: this test doesn't replace
   it, but whichever the Filer sees first is the one used. The simplest
   is to restart, then open this folder before anything else that has
   ELF programs.
2. Open this folder, so the Filer sees !SharedLibs (and !Geany).
3. Double-click !Geany. The hourglass shows while the libraries load;
   its icon goes on the icon bar and the window opens.
4. Try: open a C file (drag it to the window or the icon bar icon), edit,
   save, Find, the Symbols list, Build > Compile if you have GCC.

What to report
--------------
- Whether it starts. If not, any error box, and the Log:
  <Wimp$ScrapDir>.Geany.Log
- The Log's "riscos-gtk: started: ... ready after N s" line, and the
  same line from the static Geany (Geany-2.1-riscos15 from RC17) run
  the same way, for the start time.
- Memory: with Geany open, run !MemReport. It writes
  <Wimp$ScrapDir>.MemReport (each task's slot and each dynamic area's
  size) and opens it. Please do it once with this Geany and once with
  the static one. Where SOManager keeps the libraries didn't show on
  RISC OS on Linux, so this is the part we most want to see.
- Machine, RISC OS version, screen mode.

Files
-----
!Geany        the mixed-linked Geany (geany,e1f is the ELF program;
              lib holds the shared libraries)
!SharedLibs   Iris's !SharedLibs (SOManager 3.04, ld-riscos/so/2)
!MemReport   writes the memory report described above

